      "title": "Ordinal numbers",
      "summary": "Ordinal numbers tell the order or position.",
      "status": "draft",
      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "What it is",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraphs",
              "paragraphs": [
                "Ordinal numbers tell the order or position: first, second, third."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "the **first** day",
                "her **second** book",
                "the **twentieth** century"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "How it works in English",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraphs",
              "paragraphs": [
                "Most ordinals add -th to the cardinal number. Learn the first three: first, second and third. Five becomes fifth, eight becomes eighth, nine becomes ninth and twelve becomes twelfth."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "html": "<table><thead><tr><th>Cardinal</th><th>Ordinal</th><th>Short</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>one</strong></td><td><strong>first</strong></td><td>1st</td></tr><tr><td><strong>two</strong></td><td><strong>second</strong></td><td>2nd</td></tr><tr><td><strong>three</strong></td><td><strong>third</strong></td><td>3rd</td></tr><tr><td><strong>four</strong></td><td><strong>fourth</strong></td><td>4th</td></tr><tr><td><strong>twenty</strong></td><td><strong>twentieth</strong></td><td>20th</td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
